{
 "sheet": 1,
 "name": "LM329BZ#PBF",
 "kind": "voltage_reference",
 "manufacturer": "Analog Devices (Linear Technology)",
 "title": "6.9 V temperature-compensated precision Zener reference",
 "source": {
  "revision": "Rev D, December 2014",
  "pages": 8
 },
 "summary": "The LM129 and LM329 are two-terminal 6.9 V shunt references built on a buried Zener, which avoids the surface noise of ordinary Zeners, combined with an on-chip high-gain shunt regulator that gives a dynamic impedance of 0.6 Ω typ (LM129) or 0.8 Ω typ (LM329) at 1 mA. They run from 0.6 mA to 15 mA of reverse current and come in tempco grades from 10 ppm/°C (A) to 100 ppm/°C (LM329D). The LM329 covers 0 °C to 70 °C in a TO-92 or TO-46 can; the LM129 (-55 °C to 125 °C) and the TO-46 can are obsolete.",
 "key_figures": [
